{{!-- Roll Configuration Window Template    roll-config-label       --}}
<div class="window-roll-normal foundry-style-window">
  {{!-- Unified Header.

       No `subtitle` is passed. `rollSubtitle` is the roll type, the DC and the
       group-roll flag strung together, and this window shows all three elsewhere;
       the actor's name alone is what the caption is for. `rollSubtitle` itself is
       NOT dropped -- orchestrateRoll reads it as `skillName` for the chat card, so
       it is passed over here rather than stopped at the source.

       The comment sits out here on purpose: Handlebars does not allow a comment
       inside a partial invocation, and one placed among the parameters below is a
       parse error that takes the whole window down. --}}
  {{> "blacksmith-unified-header"
      diceIcon=diceIcon
      mainTitle=rollTitle
      dcValue=dcValue
      hasDC=hasDC
      isReadOnly=true
      showToggles=false
      actorName=actorName
      actorPortrait=actorPortrait
  }}
  
  {{!-- No "Formula" label: the row is a formula, which the dice in it say plainly.
        The clear lives here rather than among the builder buttons because what it
        clears is this line, and a control belongs with the thing it acts on. --}}
  {{!-- TOOL ROW. Configuration of the roll, sitting between the header (who and
        what) and the formula it changes.

        Roll Mode moved down here from the header to sit beside Ability, because
        they are the same kind of thing -- decisions about THIS roll -- and the core
        dnd5e dialog groups them the same way. The header is left saying who is
        rolling and what for. --}}
  <div class="roll-tools">
    {{#if abilityChoices}}
    <label class="roll-tool">
      <span class="label-small">Ability</span>
      <select name="ability" class="blacksmith-select roll-ability-select">
        {{#each abilityChoices}}
        <option value="{{this.key}}" {{#if this.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{this.label}}</option>
        {{/each}}
      </select>
    </label>
    {{/if}}
    <label class="roll-tool">
      <span class="label-small">Roll Mode</span>
      <select name="rollMode" class="blacksmith-select">
        <option value="roll" {{#if (eq rollMode "roll")}}selected{{/if}}>Public Roll</option>
        <option value="gmroll" {{#if (eq rollMode "gmroll")}}selected{{/if}}>Private GM Roll</option>
        <option value="blindroll" {{#if (eq rollMode "blindroll")}}selected{{/if}}>Blind GM Roll</option>
        <option value="selfroll" {{#if (eq rollMode "selfroll")}}selected{{/if}}>Self Roll</option>
      </select>
    </label>
  </div>

  <div class="roll-summary-row">
    <div class="roll-summary-item roll-formula-row">
      <span class="roll-formula">{{rollFormula}}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  {{#if rollAdvantageLabel}}
  <div class="roll-requested-mode{{#if lockRollAdvantage}} locked{{/if}}">
    <i class="fas fa-{{#if lockRollAdvantage}}lock{{else}}circle-info{{/if}}"></i>
    <span>Requested: <strong>{{rollAdvantageLabel}}</strong>{{#unless lockRollAdvantage}} (you may still choose){{/unless}}</span>
  </div>
  {{/if}}
  
  <div class="roll-body-scroll">
    {{!-- ONE modifier field, not two.

          There were two -- "Situational Bonus" (a number input, -20..20) and
          "Custom Modifier" (free text) -- which looked identical and accepted
          completely different things: only the second took dice, so the only way
          to add Guidance was to know that. One field, and it takes everything.

          `situational-bonus` has NOT gone away as a concept: a GM can still attach
          one per actor when requesting a roll, and it arrives pre-filled here. --}}
    <div class="roll-section">
      {{!-- The framework's section header, with its right-hand action slot, rather
            than a label and a tag-shaped button invented here. --}}
      <div class="blacksmith-window-section-header">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-plus-minus"></i>
        <span>Bonus and Modifiers</span>
        {{#if canEditPresets}}
        <button type="button" class="blacksmith-window-section-header-action roll-preset-add"
                data-tooltip="Save a new named bonus. Shared with the whole table.">
          <i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i> New
        </button>
        {{/if}}
      </div>

      {{!-- The clear sits INSIDE the field, because what it clears is the field.
            It was in the formula row, which reads as clearing the formula -- but
            the formula includes the base roll and the ability and proficiency
            terms, none of which this removes or could. --}}
      <div class="roll-modifier-field">
        <input type="text" id="roll-modifier" class="roll-modifier" name="modifier"
               value="{{modifier}}"
               placeholder="+2, 1d4, -1 — separate several with spaces"
               data-tooltip="Anything Foundry can roll: a flat bonus like +2, dice like 1d4 for Guidance, or several separated by spaces.">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-xmark roll-modifier-clear" data-tooltip="Clear the bonuses and modifiers"></i>
      </div>

      {{!-- DICE FIRST, then the named bonuses.

            The dice are a fixed, complete set -- eight faces and two operators --
            so they get one row that always shows all of them. The named list grows
            without limit, so it is the one that scrolls. Putting the scrolling row
            second also means the fixed row never moves as the list changes.

            Advantage and disadvantage are the three buttons in the footer, so keep
            highest and keep lowest are not offered here: the same ruling reached by
            two controls that can disagree is worse than one control. No multiply or
            divide either, because these only ever append a term and would introduce
            operator precedence into an expression read at a glance. --}}
      <div class="roll-builder-row">
        {{#each dice}}
        <i class="{{this.icon}} roll-builder-die" data-token="{{this.token}}" data-tooltip="{{this.tooltip}}"></i>
        {{/each}}
        <i class="fa-solid fa-plus roll-builder-op" data-op="+" data-tooltip="Add the next term"></i>
        <i class="fa-solid fa-minus roll-builder-op" data-op="-" data-tooltip="Subtract the next term"></i>
      </div>

      <div class="roll-presets" data-tooltip="Click to add. The name travels with the value, so the formula says what each term is for.">
        {{#each presets}}
        <button type="button" class="roll-preset blacksmith-tag" data-index="{{@index}}" data-value="{{this.value}}" data-label="{{this.label}}">
          {{this.label}} <span class="roll-preset-value">{{this.value}}</span>
        </button>
        {{/each}}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  <div class="roll-footer blacksmith-actions-fill">
    {{#if showDisadvantageButton}}
    <button type="button" class="blacksmith-window-btn-secondary roll-btn roll-disadvantage{{#if isDisadvantageRequested}} is-requested{{/if}}"><i class="fas fa-circle-minus"></i> Disadvantage</button>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if showNormalButton}}
    <button type="button" class="blacksmith-window-btn-secondary roll-btn roll-normal{{#if isNormalRequested}} is-requested{{/if}}"><i class="fas fa-dice-d20"></i> Normal</button>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if showAdvantageButton}}
    <button type="button" class="blacksmith-window-btn-secondary roll-btn roll-advantage{{#if isAdvantageRequested}} is-requested{{/if}}"><i class="fas fa-circle-plus"></i> Advantage</button>
    {{/if}}
  </div>
</div>
